 "balls": {},
 "id": "sb-korea-38th-short2",
 "short": true,
 "film": true,
 "photosFrom": "sb-korea-38th",
 "title": "Do You Know Korea Was Almost Split on the SAME Line 40 Years Earlier? #shorts",
 "intro": {
  "mood": "tension",
  "beats": [
   {
    "say": "Do you know Korea's border was almost drawn on the very same line, forty years before the Americans drew it?",
    "scene": {
     "shot": "card",
     "time": "40 YEARS EARLIER",
     "place": "THE SAME PARALLEL",
     "date": "Japan and Russia",
     "size": 140
    },
    "cam": {
     "lon": 127.0,
     "lat": 38.0,
     "scale": 4500
    }
   },
   {
    "say": "August 1945. Two American colonels, Dean Rusk and Charles Bonesteel, choose the thirty-eighth parallel to split Korea.",
    "scene": {
     "shot": "photo",
     "img": "bonesteel",
     "move": "in",
     "caption": "Charles H. Bonesteel III"
    }
   },
   {
    "talk": [
     {
      "who": "RUSK",
      "text": "Seoul stays on our side."
     },
     {
      "who": "BONE",
      "text": "Then the thirty-eighth it is."
     }
    ],
    "bg": {
     "shot": "set",
     "time": "night",
     "parts": [
      {
       "type": "room",
       "flag": "us",
       "window": 0.1,
       "night": true,
       "depth": 0.3
      },
      {
       "type": "table",
       "lamp": 0.5,
       "candles": 1,
       "papers": 8,
       "w": 900,
       "depth": 0.6
      }
     ]
    }
   },
   {
    "say": "What they did not know: about forty years earlier, Japan and the Russian Empire had already discussed sharing Korea. Along the same parallel.",
    "scene": {
     "shot": "doc",
     "kind": "letter",
     "header": "Japan and Russia, 40 years earlier (paraphrase)",
     "lines": [
      "Korea, shared",
      "along the 38th parallel"
     ],
     "hl": 1
    }
   },
   {
    "say": "Korea was never asked either time.",
    "scene": {
     "shot": "set",
     "time": "day",
     "parts": [
      {
       "type": "hills",
       "y": 0.5,
       "n": 3,
       "seed": 128,
       "depth": 0.15
      },
      {
       "type": "farm",
       "x": 0.3,
       "s": 0.7,
       "y": 0.72,
       "night": false,
       "depth": 0.6
      },
      {
       "type": "land",
       "kind": "grass",
       "y": 0.76,
       "depth": 0.6
      },
      {
       "type": "people",
       "list": [
        {
         "x": 0.36,
         "facing": 1,
         "h": 0.85,
         "preset": "korean",
         "pose": "point"
        },
        {
         "x": 0.62,
         "facing": -1,
         "h": 0.82,
         "preset": "woman",
         "spec": {
          "hair": "#1c1a1a",
          "skin": "#efc49c",
          "coat": "#e8e2d4"
         }
        }
       ],
       "lx": 0.4,
       "ly": 0.6,
       "depth": 0.8
      }
     ]
    }
   },
   {
    "say": "Years later, Rusk admitted it. If he had known Korean history, he said, he would almost surely have chosen a different line.",
    "scene": {
     "shot": "doc",
     "kind": "letter",
     "header": "Dean Rusk, later",
     "lines": [
      "...almost surely,",
      "have chosen a different line."
     ],
     "hl": 0
    }
   },
   {
    "say": "He did not. And that line split a country for more than eighty years.",
    "scene": {
     "shot": "photo",
     "img": "dmz",
     "move": "out",
     "caption": "DMZ fence, August 1968"
    },
    "pause": 1.0
   }
  ]
 },
